how can you define bean in spring framework
In the Spring Framework, a bean is any object that is managed by the Spring IoC (Inversion of Control) container. 
There are several ways to define beans
1.Using stereotype annotations
2.Using @Bean inside a @Configuration class

Used when:
You want full control over bean creation
You are using third-party classes
You need custom initialization logic

@Configuration
public class AppConfig {

    @Bean
    public UserService userService() {
        return new UserService();
    }
}

3. Using XML configuration 
<bean id="userService" class="com.example.UserService"/>


